# Global Constraints
- Do not invent code, APIs, properties, or library methods.
- If an API or feature is unknown, say "I do not know" instead of guessing.
- Never write infinite loops. Always include explicit exit conditions.
- Do not use placeholder code or "// TODO: implement later" comments. Write full logic.

# iOS (Swift & Xcode) Constraints
- Use only official, verified Apple Documentation for SwiftUI and UIKit.
- Target iOS 17+ features only unless specified; do not guess deprecated APIs.
- Strict Memory Management: Avoid retain cycles. Always use [weak self] in closures where necessary.
- Do not invent SF Symbols names. Only use verified Apple SF Symbols.

# Web PWA Constraints
- Use standard, widely supported Web APIs for Service Workers and Manifest files.
- Do not invent custom browser capabilities; stick strictly to HTTPS-supported PWA features.
- Ensure all loops handling DOM elements or service worker events have explicit timeouts or error catches.
